//? Title: Brent rho: actual gcd batches and a separately labelled forward orbit
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Study the actual native producer from a tiny, inspectable example through the
retained original experiment and explicit boundary/work controls. Complete
editable C++ programs own every rendered native figure.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and scope

The actual Brent splitter advances one cursor in doubling ranges, multiplies
absolute differences into batches, and tests gcds of the accumulated product. A
full gcd collapse revisits the saved block one step at a time. Modular squaring
and addition both preserve the entire uint64 range, and a selected evaluation
cap bounds a complete factorization. The original projected forward orbit
illustrates a hidden cycle but is a separately labelled native fixture, not
Brent’s actual cursor path. The original8051,12,600851475143 and prime1000000007
cases remain.

$$ f_c(x)=(x^2+c)\bmod n,\qquad q\leftarrow q|x-y|\bmod n,\qquad d=\gcd(q,n). $$

> A tiny actual producing history

The table reads actual producing records. The native diagram names actual
captured values from that same run.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pollard_rho_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/modular_exponentiation.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/integer_arithmetic.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <climits>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/number_theory.hpp>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/pollard_rho.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    auto t = dm::algorithms::pollard_rho_factor_trace(8051);
    std::print("\n| actual modulus | c | saved x | current y | actual product/difference | actual gcd | batch " "length | fallback |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t i =
         0; i < std::min<std::size_t>(6, t.history.gcds.size()); ++i) {
        auto &r = t.history.gcds[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", r.modulus,
                   r.constant, r.x, r.y, r.product, r.divisor, r.steps,
                   r.fallback);
    }

    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual first polynomial call\n{} to{}",
                       t.history.evaluations[0].before,
                       t.history.evaluations[0].after));
    d.node("n1", {9, 0},
           std::format("Actual first batch gcd\nproduct{}, gcd{}",
                       t.history.gcds[0].product, t.history.gcds[0].divisor));
    d.node("n2", {18, 0},
           std::format("Actual returned proper factor\n{}", t.factor));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/pollard_rho_tiny.svg");
}
```
